      "message": "**File:** `util/egis/bootrom.cc`\n\nIn `ExtractSecureData`, there is a dangerous integer underflow vulnerability if the device returns a response smaller than `min_resp_size` but larger than `sizeof(SecureResponseHeader)`:\n\n```c\n  // If raw_response.size() \u003c min_resp_size, this subtraction underflows\n  // to a massive unsigned value.\n  if (rsp_wrapped_len \u003e raw_response.size() - min_resp_size) {\n    rsp_wrapped_len \u003d raw_response.size() - min_resp_size;\n  }\n\n```\n\nIf an underflow occurs, `rsp_wrapped_len` is not clamped correctly, and the subsequent `raw_response.subspan(...)` call will either throw an out-of-bounds exception or cause Undefined Behavior.\n\n**Remediation:** Add a strict size check at the top of the function immediately after validating the header:\n\n```c\n  if (raw_response.size() \u003c min_resp_size) {\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  }\n\n```",
